     "explanation": "Sinclair's three predictions are: (1) an FDA-approved aging drug, (2) routine biological age testing, and (3) people alive now reaching 120 in good health. He has not advocated mandatory genome editing.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox='0 0 1100 1100' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'><rect width='1100' height='1100' fill='#1a1a2e'/><text x='550' y='70' fill='#FFD700' font-size='36' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='bold'>Quiz: Predictions</text><text x='550' y='115' fill='#888' font-size='24' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle'>Which one is not Sinclair's?</text><rect x='100' y='200' width='900' height='320' fill='#1a1a2e' stroke='#0ea5e9' stroke-width='2' rx='12'/><text x='550' y='250' fill='#0ea5e9' font-size='26' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='bold'>The Three Predictions</text><text x='150' y='310' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>1. Drug approved that targets aging</text><text x='150' y='360' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>2. Biological age tests routine in clinic</text><text x='150' y='410' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>3. Living humans reach 120 in good health</text><text x='150' y='470' fill='#888' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>Note: he is silent on coercive genetic policy.</text><rect x='100' y='560' width='900' height='220' fill='#1a1a2e' stroke='#FFD700' stroke-width='2' rx='12'/><text x='550' y='605' fill='#FFD700' font-size='26' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='bold'>Why Falsifiable Matters</text><text x='150' y='655' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>These claims have clear timelines and metrics.</text><text x='150' y='690' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>That is what separates science from speculation.</text><text x='150' y='725' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>You can hold Sinclair accountable to them.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Falsifiable claims are testable claims."
     }
