    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: Design Your Diet Experiment",
     "content": "Design a 4-week diet experiment on yourself. Specify the intervention (e.g., 16:8 IF, plant-forward, methionine-aware), the baseline measurements, the weekly tracked metrics, and how you will judge success. (No nutrition coaching here — this is a study design exercise.)",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox='0 0 1100 1100' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'><rect width='1100' height='1100' fill='#1a1a2e'/><text x='550' y='70' fill='#FFD700' font-size='36' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='bold'>Practice 1: N=1 Trial</text><text x='550' y='115' fill='#888' font-size='24' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle'>Design a self-experiment</text><rect x='100' y='180' width='900' height='200' fill='#1a1a2e' stroke='#0ea5e9' stroke-width='2' rx='12'/><text x='550' y='225' fill='#0ea5e9' font-size='26' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='bold'>Step 1: Choose intervention</text><text x='150' y='275' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>16:8 TRE, 5:2 IF, ~10% CR, plant-forward,</text><text x='150' y='310' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>methionine-aware, fasting-mimicking diet</text><text x='150' y='345' fill='#888' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>Choose ONE so you can attribute changes.</text><rect x='100' y='400' width='900' height='220' fill='#1a1a2e' stroke='#FFD700' stroke-width='2' rx='12'/><text x='550' y='445' fill='#FFD700' font-size='26' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='bold'>Step 2: Measurements</text><text x='150' y='495' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>Baseline + final: weight, BP, fasting glucose</text><text x='150' y='530' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>Weekly: sleep quality, energy, mood</text><text x='150' y='565' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>Optional: HRV, resting HR, basic lipid panel</text><text x='150' y='600' fill='#888' font-size='18' font-family='Arial'>Use validated apps where possible.</text><rect x='100' y='640' width='900' height='300' fill='#1a1a2e' stroke='#8b5cf6' stroke-width='2' rx='12'/><text x='550' y='685' fill='#8b5cf6' font-size='26' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='bold'>Step 3: Analysis plan</text><text x='150' y='735' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>Define \"success\" in advance</text><text x='150' y='770' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>Plan for placebo + novelty effects</text><text x='150' y='805' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>Document confounders (illness, travel)</text><text x='150' y='840' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>What would convince you to keep going?</text><text x='150' y='875' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>What would convince you to stop?</text><text x='150' y='915' fill='#888' font-size='18' font-family='Arial'>Deliverable: 2-page protocol. Discuss in seminar.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "N=1 is not real evidence, but it teaches study design."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: Rapamycin Risk-Benefit Memo",
     "content": "Imagine a 55-year-old healthy patient asks for off-label rapamycin. Write a 1-page memo summarizing: current evidence, dosing protocols studied, known side effects, monitoring required, alternatives. Decide whether you would prescribe and why.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox='0 0 1100 1100' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'><rect width='1100' height='1100' fill='#1a1a2e'/><text x='550' y='70' fill='#FFD700' font-size='36' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='bold'>Practice 2: Rapamycin Memo</text><text x='550' y='115' fill='#888' font-size='24' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle'>Off-label decision-making</text><rect x='100' y='180' width='900' height='180' fill='#1a1a2e' stroke='#0ea5e9' stroke-width='2' rx='12'/><text x='550' y='225' fill='#0ea5e9' font-size='26' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='bold'>Scenario</text><text x='150' y='275' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>55 yo, healthy, normal labs, no insurance issue</text><text x='150' y='310' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>Read Lifespan, requesting rapamycin</text><text x='150' y='345' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>Wants to know your recommendation</text><rect x='100' y='380' width='900' height='240' fill='#1a1a2e' stroke='#FFD700' stroke-width='2' rx='12'/><text x='550' y='425' fill='#FFD700' font-size='26' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='bold'>Required content</text><text x='150' y='475' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>1. Animal evidence summary</text><text x='150' y='510' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>2. Human trial summary (Mannick, PEARL, others)</text><text x='150' y='545' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>3. Side effect catalog</text><text x='150' y='580' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>4. Suggested dosing if you said yes</text><rect x='100' y='640' width='900' height='160' fill='#1a1a2e' stroke='#8b5cf6' stroke-width='2' rx='12'/><text x='550' y='685' fill='#8b5cf6' font-size='26' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='bold'>Required Sections</text><text x='150' y='735' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>5. Monitoring schedule (labs, frequency)</text><text x='150' y='770' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial'>6. Stop criteria</text><rect x='100' y='820' width='900' height='120' fill='#1a1a2e' stroke='#ef4444' stroke-width='2' rx='12'/><text x='550' y='870' fill='#ef4444' font-size='26' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='bold'>Bottom line</text><text x='550' y='910' fill='#FFFFFF' font-size='22' font-family='Arial' text-anchor='middle'>Decide and defend. State your reasoning.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Off-label decisions are real-world clinical reasoning."
     }
    }
